================================================================================
 AGENT SKILLS CHEATSHEET                                         idea -> ship
================================================================================

 THINKING: WHICH ONE?
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /grill-with-docs   Sharpen an idea by interview, IN a repo. Stateful: writes
                    GLOSSARY.md + ADRs as it goes. Default start of a feature.
 /grill-me          Same interview, NO repo. Saves nothing. Plans, writing,
                    naming the project.
 /domain-modeling   The WORDS are the problem: fuzzy or overloaded term, naming
                    a feature/concept, editing GLOSSARY.md, recording an ADR.
 /codebase-design   The SHAPE is the problem: where a seam goes, how deep a
                    module is, what its interface exposes. Reference, not a
                    session. Vocabulary only: no naming guidance.

   in a repo? --no--> /grill-me
       | yes
   whole idea fuzzy? --yes--> /grill-with-docs   (drives /domain-modeling)
       | no
       +-- one word unclear ---------> /domain-modeling
       +-- one module's shape -------> /codebase-design

 MAIN FLOW
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   /grill-with-docs --> [/prototype if a question needs running code]
          |
     multi-session build?
          +-- no  --> /implement                       (same context window)
          +-- yes --> /to-spec --> /to-tickets
                         +--> /implement per ticket, /clear between each
                         +--> /implement-spec  (parallel agents, one branch)

   /implement = /tdd + /code-review   -->   /pr   -->   /retro

 FEEDING THE THINKING
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /research          WHEN: you need facts (docs, APIs, specs), not opinions.
                    HOW:  give it one question. A background agent reads
                          PRIMARY sources and writes one cited .md in the repo.
                          Keep working meanwhile; take the file into a grill.
 /prototype         WHEN: a design question won't settle on paper.
                    HOW:  logic/state -> one clickable HTML file;
                          UI -> several variants on one route. Throwaway code;
                          keep it on a side branch, fold the answer into main.
 /to-questionnaire  WHEN: the answer is in someone else's head.

 BUILDING AND CHECKING
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /tdd               One red -> green slice at a time. Agree the seams to test
                    BEFORE writing tests. No refactoring inside the loop.
 /code-review       Diff since a fixed point (branch, SHA, main), two separate
                    reports: Standards (repo rules + code smells) and Spec.
 /pr                Shapes the PR body. Agent reaches for it on its own.
 /retro             After a build: fix the agent's environment, not the code.

 ON-RAMPS
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /diagnosing-bugs   Hard bug. First build ONE fast command that goes red on
                    this bug; no theories before that. Then 3-5 ranked
                    hypotheses, fix, regression test.
 /triage            Raw incoming issues you didn't write -> agent-ready.
 /wayfinder         Too big and foggy for one session. Produces decisions,
                    then hands off to /to-spec. Slow; not for scoped features.
 /improve-codebase-architecture   Spare-moment upkeep; finds candidates to
                    take into /grill-with-docs.

 UTILITIES
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 /wizard            Steps only a human can do (credentials, dashboards).
 /wait-what         Last message didn't land: re-pitch in plain English.
 /handoff           Portable .md for a new directory, harness or colleague.

 CONTEXT RULES
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Grill -> spec -> tickets: ONE unbroken window. No /clear, no /compact.
 * Each /implement starts fresh from its ticket.
 * Run /retro before clearing the session it looks back on.
 * Near ~150k tokens: /compact at the next phase boundary, don't push on.
================================================================================
